## Reserving a name

```bash
# from backend/
DFX_WARNING=-mainnet_plaintext_identity \
  dfx canister call icp_wallet_backend reserveUsername '("name")' --network ic
```

Returns `(variant { ok = "name" })` on success. Errors:
- `"Not authorized"` — caller is not a controller.
- `"Username already claimed by a user"` — a user already owns it (permanent, cannot be reserved).
- `"Username is reserved"` / invalid-name messages.

## Releasing a name (removes the hold)

```bash
DFX_WARNING=-mainnet_plaintext_identity \
  dfx canister call icp_wallet_backend releaseUsername '("name")' --network ic
```

Immediately frees the name back to the open pool — the first claimer or buyer
wins it. There is no grace period or re-list backstop.

